<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12309"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 11:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsbarn: I agree with you. He may have wised up and planned to take his DNA with him. I think that his urge to kill has been building and he was toying with different situations for just the right moment where he could kill and run. He then would be in a position to interject himself into the crime scene because of his &#39;enforcer&#39; position. Who knows what lurked in his little pea brain.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
