<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12325"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 10:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Your certain this was in April of 99? I&#39;m thinking that the WPD should be scanning the park, the creek, and the water treatment plant all close to the community building for buried treasures. Was he in the process of starting taunts with the PCPD and attempting to make a drop near the building?. My family had a big graduation party for me at that building when I graduated from Heights. My sister and I used to walk to the park to the swimming pool after we mowed the lawn. And yes, this was a long ways and after DTDC moved to the area. I do remember seeing him in his lil white truck when I was taking my kids to the same pool years later. Thanks, E for shareing that with us. Tell your friend, thanks for sharing that with us and maybe she should think about forwarding that info to the PCPD.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
